    "### Jangila Rockland \n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Part 1\n",
    "* For this project, I chose a dataset from JSONLint's Free JSON Datasets link.  I chose a JSON file that had information on World Airports. \n",
    "* https://jsonlint.com/datasets/airports \n",
    "* I chose this dataset because I like to travel around the world. This dataset can provide information on which airports are potentially the best international travel hotspots. \n",
    "* Each observation represents an individual major airport around the world. This includes its airport code, name, city, country, and coordinates.\n",
    "* The variables that I plan to investigate are: \"lat\" and \"lon\" to measure the location of the airport. I will also use the variable \"Country,\" which ties in with the coordinates. I am going to create a variable to measure the distance of each airport to the others in the file to discover which airport is most centrally located. \n",
    "##### Research Question and Hypothesis:\n",
    "* Research question: Which airports have a location that is closest to other major airport hubs? Do international airports sit closer to one another than airports in the United States?\n",
    "* Hypothesis: Major airports in countries other than the United States, more specifically Europe, sit closer to other airports than US airports do, serving as easier travel hotspot destinations."
